    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., dropping from ~79 to ~63) followed by high volatility; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 10-15 EUR in the first week.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture immediate mean reversion after sharp spikes, instead predicting continued upward drift that lags behind actual price reversals.",
    "Sentiment history (values > 0.20) correlates with model overconfidence during volatile periods, leading to linear extrapolation errors rather than adaptive volatility adjustments.",
    "Model ignores the 'mean-reverting' nature of EU ETS prices during crisis phases, assuming smooth growth where true outcomes show erratic oscillations between 60-80 EUR.",
    "Forecast horizon error is systematic: predictions for days 5-10 are consistently higher than actuals by ~12 EUR due to failure to model sudden policy-driven drops."
